      "writtenOn": "2026-04-08T16:13:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The iommu_tlb_flush is called after the donated page mapped in the guest mmu. This seems can open a small window that, the other guest vcpus can access this donated memory pages while the device can also access via stale IOMMU tlb. To close this window, we can call it before map to the guest?\n\nAhh yes nice catch. I assumed that IOMMU will not have stale entries as the page was not in IOMMU page table when this happens, but a host can unmap a page and immdiately donate it and with lazy flushing we don\u0027t immediately flush so the IOMMU may really have stale entries. Will fix this",
